{"All-client permission lookups resolve the resource by the wrong key - findByName passes resource type as name and server id as resource type, not matching how the resource is created": 0.5672304630279541, "Client permission lookup returns no matches because getClientIdsByScope searches by the resource type name instead of the client resource name": 0.3513275682926178, "Client resource type is registered in the schema but not in V2 evaluation mapping, causing permissions to not be found or evaluated correctly": 0.2633497714996338, "Client listing in V2 ignores view-only client permissions by dropping the QUERY_CLIENTS/QUERY_USERS fallback used by the peer implementation": 0.2736959755420685, "Client manage check omits the self-client validation used by peers - no explicit resource lookup/validation layer in the method": 0.19571654498577118, "canView(ClientModel) ignores the explicit view permission for V2 when a client already has manage or configure rights, diverging from documented V2 semantics": 0.0969255268573761, "Client scope management in V2 is more permissive than the established client pattern - allows users with fine-grained all-client manage permission to mutate client scopes when legacy implementation would not": 0.21122220158576965, "V2 client permission examples using VIEW and MANAGE on a single client are misleading because implementation differentiates view, manage, and configure scopes separately": 0.047830965369939804, "Client resource-type permission tests do not cover the failure mode where the resource type name is wrong or the all-clients lookup returns null/wrong resource name": 0.1400335431098938, "Removed FGAP listener gating for role/client/group removals may affect non-FGAP behavior - when FGAP is disabled the listener no longer disables permissions on removed roles, clients, or groups": 0.6741893887519836}